# Run outputs. Every one of these is regenerated by run.py / the scripts in
# ModernTCN-Long-term-forecasting/scripts, and each new run overwrites the last,
# so tracking them would put one machine's results into version control and make
# every rerun a diff.
#
#   checkpoints/    best-epoch weights, one directory per setting string
#   results/        per-setting metrics, forecasts and pred.npy
#   test_results/   per-setting forecast plots
#   result*.txt     the append-only loss log test() writes
#   results_optuna/ tune_optuna.py's best params, trial table and command
checkpoints/
results/
test_results/
result.txt
result_rv.txt
results_optuna/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
